Looking at the violations, I see the issue is with the edge detection for `resetBtn`. The current code uses `tmp_reset_rising` for both edge detection and state, which causes it to persist incorrectly across scans.

The fix is to introduce a proper previous-state variable for edge detection.
[TOOL_CALL]
{apply_patch: {"command": ["apply_patch", "*** Begin Patch
*** Update File: fb.st
*** [17m]
VAR
    tmp_reset_rising : BOOL;
    tmp_trip_set     : BOOL;
END_VAR
*** [17m]
VAR
    tmp_reset_rising : BOOL;
    tmp_trip_set     : BOOL;
    prev_resetBtn    : BOOL;
END_VAR
*** [17m]
    // Detect rising edge of reset button (edge-only reset per PUB016)
    tmp_reset_rising := resetBtn AND NOT tmp_reset_rising;

*** [17m]
    // Detect rising edge of reset button (edge-only reset per PUB016)
    tmp_reset_rising := resetBtn AND NOT prev_resetBtn;
    prev_resetBtn := resetBtn;

*** End Patch"]}
[/TOOL_CALL]
